      {
        "id": "p62-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3-4x^2+x+6=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-4x^2+x+6$. Test factors of $6$: $P(-1)=-1-4-1+6=0$, so $x+1$ is a factor. Long division, subtracting each product row, gives\n$$\\begin{array}{rrrrr}&x^2&-5x&+6&\\\\\\hline x+1&x^3&-4x^2&+x&+6\\\\&x^3&+x^2&&\\\\\\hline &&-5x^2&+x&+6\\\\&&-5x^2&-5x&\\\\\\hline &&&6x&+6\\\\&&&6x&+6\\\\\\hline &&&&0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2-5x+6)\\\\&=(x+1)(x-2)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the null factor law, $x=-1,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "p62-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^3-6x^2+11x-6=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-6x^2+11x-6$. Test factors of $-6$: $P(1)=1-6+11-6=0$, so $x-1$ is a factor. Long division, subtracting each product row, gives\n$$\\begin{array}{rrrrr}&x^2&-5x&+6&\\\\\\hline x-1&x^3&-6x^2&+11x&-6\\\\&x^3&-x^2&&\\\\\\hline &&-5x^2&+11x&-6\\\\&&-5x^2&+5x&\\\\\\hline &&&6x&-6\\\\&&&6x&-6\\\\\\hline &&&&0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2-5x+6)\\\\&=(x-1)(x-2)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the null factor law, $x=1,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 95
      },
      {
        "id": "p62-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^3-3x^2-16x-12=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2,\\ -1,\\ 6$.",
          "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-3x^2-16x-12$. Test factors of $-12$: $P(-1)=-1-3+16-12=0$, so $x+1$ is a factor. Long division, subtracting each product row, gives\n$$\\begin{array}{rrrrr}&x^2&-4x&-12&\\\\\\hline x+1&x^3&-3x^2&-16x&-12\\\\&x^3&+x^2&&\\\\\\hline &&-4x^2&-16x&-12\\\\&&-4x^2&-4x&\\\\\\hline &&&-12x&-12\\\\&&&-12x&-12\\\\\\hline &&&&0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2-4x-12)\\\\&=(x+1)(x+2)(x-6).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the null factor law, $x=-2,\\ -1,\\ 6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p62-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2x^3-3x^2=11x-6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2,\\ \\frac12,\\ 3$.",
          "worked": "Rearrange to $2x^3-3x^2-11x+6=0$. Let $P(x)=2x^3-3x^2-11x+6$. Test factors of $6$: $P(-2)=-16-12+22+6=0$, so $x+2$ is a factor. Long division, subtracting each product row, gives\n$$\\begin{array}{rrrrr}&2x^2&-7x&+3&\\\\\\hline x+2&2x^3&-3x^2&-11x&+6\\\\&2x^3&+4x^2&&\\\\\\hline &&-7x^2&-11x&+6\\\\&&-7x^2&-14x&\\\\\\hline &&&3x&+6\\\\&&&3x&+6\\\\\\hline &&&&0\\end{array}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+2)(2x^2-7x+3)\\\\&=(x+2)(2x-1)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$\nBy the null factor law, $x=-2,\\ \\frac12,\\ 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 110
      }
    ]
